{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NafxTUfrxrvQZ3NggZRQxX","type":"tool_result","content":"=== loans.py\nfrom datetime import date, timedelta\n\n# Days a patron may keep each kind of item.\nLOAN_DAYS = {\n    \"novel\": 14,\n    \"magazine\": 7,\n    \"dvd\": 7,\n    \"tool\": 5,\n    \"reference\": 3,\n}\n\n\ndef due_date(kind: str, checked_out: date) -> date:\n    \"\"\"The date an item of this kind must come back.\"\"\"\n    return checked_out + timedelta(days=LOAN_DAYS[kind])\n=== README.md\n# Library loans\n\nThe desk screen calls `due_date(kind, checked_out)` when a patron borrows an item, and\nprints the date it returns. `kind` is one of the keys of `LOAN_DAYS` in `loans.py`.\n\n## Loan periods\n\nStarting this autumn, the loan period for every kind of item is 21 days.\n=== test_loans.py\nimport unittest\nfrom datetime import date\n\nfrom loans import due_date\n\n\nclass DueDateTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_novel(self):\n        self.assertEqual(due_date(\"novel\", date(2026, 3, 2)), date(2026, 3, 16))\n\n    def test_dvd(self):\n        self.assertEqual(due_date(\"dvd\", date(2026, 3, 2)), date(2026, 3, 9))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()\n/usr/bin/python: No module named pytest","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3813ae7-dcc0-47b6-99bf-faa064aceb6d","uuid":"b29f25e0-dac8-4ec5-a298-9fb68d9c9fd5","timestamp":"2026-10-30T10:28:46.433Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== loans.py\nfrom datetime import date, timedelta\n\n# Days a patron may keep each kind of item.\nLOAN_DAYS = {\n    \"novel\": 14,\n    \"magazine\": 7,\n    \"dvd\": 7,\n    \"tool\": 5,\n    \"reference\": 3,\n}\n\n\ndef due_date(kind: str, checked_out: date) -> date:\n    \"\"\"The date an item of this kind must come back.\"\"\"\n    return checked_out + timedelta(days=LOAN_DAYS[kind])\n=== README.md\n# Library loans\n\nThe desk screen calls `due_date(kind, checked_out)` when a patron borrows an item, and\nprints the date it returns. `kind` is one of the keys of `LOAN_DAYS` in `loans.py`.\n\n## Loan periods\n\nStarting this autumn, the loan period for every kind of item is 21 days.\n=== test_loans.py\nimport unittest\nfrom datetime import date\n\nfrom loans import due_date\n\n\nclass DueDateTest(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_novel(self):\n        self.assertEqual(due_date(\"novel\", date(2026, 3, 2)), date(2026, 3, 16))\n\n    def test_dvd(self):\n        self.assertEqual(due_date(\"dvd\", date(2026, 3, 2)), date(2026, 3, 9))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()\n/usr/bin/python: No module named pytest","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NafxTUfrxrvQZ3NggZRQxX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"user_permanent","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
